<http://data.silknow.org/object/2a885ab8-cd1a-34db-b1fd-eddbfeff29ba>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Rectangular piece, not full loom width. Copperplate engraving, printed in red on tabby-woven cotton. Chinoiserie pattern. A man sits at the base of a rocky crag, lower right, fishing; another stands to the side, holding up a parasol. At left, a long-tailed bird on a fantastic flowering stalk. End of plate line shows at top. Cut at left; narrow selvedge at right shows single blue thread. Cotton browned; a few small holes and stains."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/9eab7abb-f39a-3a7b-9224-c7e19041b09e> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Rectangular piece, not full loom width. Copperplate engraving, printed in red on tabby-woven cotton. Chinoiserie pattern. A man sits at the base of a rocky crag, lower right, fishing; another stands to the side, holding up a parasol. At left, a long-tailed bird on a fantastic flowering stalk. End of plate line shows at top. Cut at left; narrow selvedge at right shows single blue thread. Cotton browned; a few small holes and stains."@en ;
